Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Window Four Keeps the Second Note
- Story & Context: At 134 BPM, Ingrid opens with a three-note fiddle hook built from tonic, fifth, and minor third. Caio places a compact tamborzão cell beneath it but removes upper percussion after the second note. The bowed phrase ends quickly; the sympathetic microphone continues carrying a faint fifth and octave for nearly another bar. Liv waits until that afterimage disappears before striking one prepared-vibraphone suspended-second dyad. João replaces the second clap of every fourth bar with a dry woodblock. Elise enters only during the first Shadow Chord section, where electric bass drops out and a low bass-clarinet breath tone sits beneath the residual fiddle resonance. The hook depends on hearing a note continue after the bow has visibly left it.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Frosted ferry service window marked 4, one sharp black note symbol with a pale duplicate drifting behind it, brass ticket punch on a worn counter, dark water beyond the glass. Sparse lyric fragments: “window four,” “second note stays,” “cut the bow,” “shadow keeps it.”

Track 2: Route Ledger Printed the Drone Wrong
- Story & Context: At 138 BPM, Ingrid repeats the same five-note bowed figure across three sections while changing only which open strings remain free. The first pass leaves tonic and fifth resonating; the second frees an upper second; the third introduces a darker minor-seventh shadow. Caio keeps the principal drum and bass pattern nearly identical so the harmonic change is carried by Drone Misprint rather than chord progression. Liv contributes clipped vibraphone octaves only after each resonance field clears. João uses surdo rim to mark each new open-string configuration. In the middle section, Dry Cut / Wet Memory removes the direct fiddle abruptly while the sympathetic channel persists alone beneath kick and clap.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Old ferry route ledger with one line printed three times but each copy carrying a different faint background color, dark fiddle strings crossing the page, stamped route number partly blurred. Sparse lyric fragments: “same route,” “drone printed wrong,” “leave this string,” “memory changes.”

Track 3: Last Crossing After the Bow Is Gone
- Story & Context: The closer runs at 128 BPM and begins with no electric bass. Ingrid plays isolated double-stops separated by long silence, allowing each sympathetic field to decay almost completely before the next phrase. Caio uses only kick, one clipped clap, and occasional low drum punctuation. Elise supplies low chalumeau pedals beneath the longest Shadow Chord sections. Liv remains silent for the first two minutes, then enters with one damped minor-seventh vibraphone shell after the clearest resonance fade on the EP. In the final minute, Ingrid plays one low open-string drone and then physically lifts the bow away. Caio removes every drum layer except a single kick. The sympathetic strings continue trembling underneath the body microphone until they fall below the room noise. The final kick never arrives.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Empty ferry departure hall after closing, one violin bow resting on a wooden bench while an ornate Hardanger fiddle remains upright nearby, faint reflected route lettering in frosted glass, dark water and one distant dock light outside. Sparse lyric fragments: “last crossing,” “bow is gone,” “still ringing,” “no last kick.”

